{
  "name": "Thinking About Moving a Wall? Here's What You Need to Know First",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about moving or adding an interior wall can open up so many possibilities for your space, but it's not always as simple as just putting up some studs. The first thing you absolutely need to figure out is whether that wall is load-bearing. This is huge! A load-bearing wall supports the weight of your home's structure, and messing with it without proper planning can have serious consequences. If it's just a partition wall, it's a bit simpler, but you still need to think about things like whether the new wall will line up nicely with your ceiling and floor framing. Sometimes, existing drywall might even need to come down to properly tie in the new framing. Establishing layout lines on your floor and ceiling is the very first step, then you'll cut your top and bottom plates and studs to fit. After that, it's about assembling the wall, making sure it's plumb (perfectly vertical) and shimmed correctly before fastening it securely. This is where precision really matters. For anything beyond a simple partition, especially if you're unsure about the structural implications or local regulations, it's always a good idea to chat with an expert. HH Remodeling can help you navigate these initial questions and ensure your project starts off right.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
